            "review_title": "Review at Ba Con Cuu Cao Thang",
            "review_text": "Martin n\nSydney, Australia305 contributions\n0\nDon't judge a book by its cover\nJun 2016 • Friends\nWe were invited to this restaurant by friends who recommended the Mongolian hot pot. Unfortunately, we didn't get that far because although the decor and prices are upmarket, the level of attentiveness from staff is at the opposite end of the scale!\nWe asked for any one of the three Chilean wines on the menu but were told they were out of stock and only the Argentinian wine was available (at almost double the price!). When we insisted on Chilean wine, we were told to wait 15 minutes while someone went out to get some - and were then ignored by all staff who passed us by as though we didn't exist! When no wine (or wait staff) had showed up 25 minutes later, we took our wallets and appetites elsewhere!\nBy all means try this restaurant because the hot pot is highly recommended - but make sure you can get what you want before you sit down!\nRead more\nService\nWritten June 9, 2016",
